      {
        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "b2d34081-cdc1-5fef-89bf-94eb6d89264f",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Products: Rosetta Stone\n- Organizations: Ptolemaic dynasty\n- Places: Memphis, Egypt; Egypt\n- People: King Ptolemy V; Ptolemy I; Lagus\n- Concepts: ancient Egyptian hieroglyphs; Hellenistic period; Ptolemaic Kingdom\n\nFacts:\n- In 196 BC, a decree was issued at Memphis, Egypt on behalf of King Ptolemy V during the Ptolemaic dynasty.\n- From 305 to 30 BC, the Ptolemaic dynasty, a Macedonian Greek royal family, ruled the Ptolemaic Kingdom in Egypt during the Hellenistic period.\n- The Ptolemaic dynasty was also known as the Lagids or Lagidae, a name derived from Lagus, the father of Ptolemy I.\n- In 1799, the Rosetta Stone, a granodiorite stele, was found with three versions of the 196 BC decree inscribed on it.\n- The discovery of the Rosetta Stone helped scholars decipher ancient Egyptian hieroglyphs.\n- The decipherment of ancient Egyptian hieroglyphs revealed much of Egypt's ancient history, which had previously been a mystery.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
        "original_id": "066d616c-0f2c-5fb3-98a9-4b37a92c50ce",
        "text": "Page: Rosetta Stone. Sentence: The Rosetta Stone is a granodiorite stele, found in 1799, inscribed with three versions of a decree issued at Memphis, Egypt in 196 BC during the Ptolemaic dynasty on behalf of King Ptolemy V.\nPage: Ptolemaic dynasty. Sentence: The Ptolemaic dynasty (Ancient Greek: Πτολεμαῖοι , \"Ptolemaioi\"), sometimes also known as the Lagids or Lagidae (Ancient Greek: Λαγίδαι , \"Lagidai\", after Lagus, Ptolemy I's father), was a Macedonian Greek royal family, which ruled the Ptolemaic Kingdom in Egypt during the Hellenistic period.\nPage: Ptolemaic dynasty. Sentence: Their rule lasted for 275 years, from 305 to 30 BC.\nPage: History of Egypt. Sentence: Much of Egypt's ancient history was a mystery until the secrets of ancient Egyptian hieroglyphs were deciphered with the discovery and help of the Rosetta Stone.",
        "type": "DocumentChunk"
